#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:2
msgid "Hardware interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:4
msgid ""
"Hardware IO (input/output) interfaces, including the {ref}`serial-port "
"<interfaces-serial-port-interface>`, {ref}`gpio <interfaces-gpio-"
"interface>`, {ref}`gpio-chardev <interfaces-gpio-chardev>` and {ref}`i2c "
"<interfaces-i2c-interface>` interfaces, are designed to be used on devices "
"running {ref}`Ubuntu Core <ref-glossary_ubuntu-core>`. These interfaces are "
"exposed as _slots_ from a device's {ref}`gadget snap <reference-development-"
"yaml-schemas-the-gadget-snap>` which is used to define and configure a "
"device's system properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:6
msgid ""
"This approach is more robust because it allows the gadget snap providing the "
"slot to centralise and arbitrate the connection conditions. These conditions "
"include which other snaps, identified by their snap ID, can connect to the "
"slots the gadget offers and, consequently, gain privileged access to the "
"hardware.  For the application snap, usually no change is required other "
"than to declare and use an appropriately-configured plug."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:9
msgid ""
"The following are exceptions to the above, and can be used without being "
"declared in the gadget snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:10
msgid "{ref}`gpio-control interface <interfaces-gpio-control-interface>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:11
msgid ""
"{ref}`serial-port interface <interfaces-serial-port-interface>` "
"(experimental support)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:13
msgid ""
"See {ref}`Supported interfaces <ref-index_interfaces>` for a complete list "
"of interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:15
msgid "Interface considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:17
msgid ""
"The extent of access an interface has is granted through both _connection "
"permissions_ and the specifics of the _interface connections_ being "
"requested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:19
msgid ""
"**Connection permissions**: {ref}`auto-connect <explanation-interfaces-"
"interface-auto-connection>` | {ref}`privileged <reference-operations-"
"interfaces-super-privileged-interfaces>` | {ref}`super-privileged <reference-"
"operations-interfaces-super-privileged-interfaces>` </br>Connection "
"requirements are dependent on which store a developer is using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:19
msgid "</br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:21
msgid ""
"{ref}`Global Snap Store <ref-glossary_snap-store>`: privileged and super-"
"privileged interfaces require store approval because of the level of trust "
"and permissiveness these interfaces have, which is also why certain "
"interfaces need certain oversight. See {ref}`Permission requests <interfaces-"
"process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks>` for further details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:22
msgid ""
"[Dedicated Snap Store](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/core/explanation/"
"stores/dedicated-snap-store): trust and permissiveness are now  the "
"responsibility of the store owner, and many privileged interface connections "
"can be self-served and defined within the dedicated snap store and the "
"device context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:23
msgid ""
"**Interface connections**: hardware IO interfaces | app-provided interfaces "
"| other interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:24
msgid ""
"**Hardware IO interfaces**: These require either a {ref}`slot <how-to-guides-"
"work-with-snaps-connect-interfaces>` to be defined by a device's _gadget "
"snap_ or an interface with {ref}`Hotplug support <interfaces-hotplug-"
"support>`, in which case the slot appears from the system snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:25
msgid ""
"An unconstrained {ref}`auto-connection <explanation-interfaces-interface-"
"auto-connection>` cannot be used because there may be _many slots of a given "
"interface_, resulting in ambiguity that requires  an extensive set of store "
"rules to manage and maintain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:26
msgid "Each plug should therefore be connected to a slot, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:27
msgid "green led plug on app => green led slot on gadget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:28
msgid "red led plug on app => red led slot on gadget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:29
msgid ""
"This kind of 1-to-1 connections can usually be established via {ref}`slot "
"rules in the snap-declaration <explanation-interfaces-interface-auto-"
"connection>` for the gadget."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:30
msgid ""
"**App-provided interfaces**: slots are defined by apps, or occasionally from "
"the gadget snap,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:31
msgid ""
"May require access, such as from the {ref}`content <interfaces-content-"
"interface>` or {ref}`shared-memory <interfaces-shared-memory-interface>` "
"interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:32
msgid ""
"A slot might may be provided by the system snap to cover the case of an "
"equivalent system service, such as {ref}`audio-playback <interfaces-audio-"
"playback-interface>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:33
msgid ""
"the slot might be {ref}`super-privileged <reference-operations-interfaces-"
"super-privileged-interfaces>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:34
msgid ""
"**Other interfaces**: For more system level access, slots are provided by "
"the system snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:36
msgid "<h3 id='heading--code-examples'>Code examples</h3>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:38
msgid ""
"The [gadget snap](https://github.com/canonical/pi-gadget/tree/20-arm64) "
"definition for the reference [Raspberry Pi Ubuntu Core](https://ubuntu.com/"
"core/docs/install-raspberry-pi) image contains interface definitions for "
"various hardware IO interfaces on the system, including slots for each "
"specific GPIO pin, i2c connections, the Bluetooth serial port, and the "
"generic serial ports:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:40
msgid ""
"slots:\n"
"  bcm-gpio-0:\n"
"    interface: gpio\n"
"    number: 0\n"
"  bcm-gpio-1:\n"
"    interface: gpio\n"
"    number: 1\n"
"  bcm-gpio-2:\n"
"    interface: gpio\n"
"    number: 2\n"
"[...]\n"
"  i2c-0:\n"
"    interface: i2c\n"
"    path: /dev/i2c-0\n"
"[...]\n"
"  bt-serial:\n"
"    interface: serial-port\n"
"    path: /dev/ttyAMA0\n"
"[...]\n"
"  serial0:\n"
"    interface: serial-port\n"
"    path: /dev/ttyS0\n"
"  serial1:\n"
"    interface: serial-port\n"
"    path: /dev/ttyS1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/interfaces/hardware-interfaces.md:68
msgid ""
"On a Raspberry Pi, the above hardware IO interfaces are accessible to apps "
"from the system snap without requiring any further configuration."
msgstr ""
